# ⚡ Electricity Consumption Forecasting

## 📌 Overview

This project focuses on forecasting household electricity consumption using time series models such as **ARIMA** and **SARIMA**.
The objective is to analyze historical consumption patterns and generate accurate future predictions for better energy planning.

---

## 📊 Dataset

* **Name:** Household Electric Power Consumption
* **Source:** Kaggle
* **Dataset Link:** https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/uciml/electric-power-consumption-data-set
* **Reference Notebook:** https://www.kaggle.com/code/nitishviraktamath/household-power-consumption
* **Size:** ~2 million records (minute-level time series data)

### 📥 How to Use Dataset

1. Download the dataset from the link above
2. Extract the file
3. Place it in the following directory:

```text
data/household_power_consumption.csv
```

> ⚠️ Note: The dataset is not included in this repository due to GitHub's 100MB file size limit.

---

## ⚙️ Features

* Data preprocessing and cleaning
* Handling missing values
* Time series visualization
* ARIMA and SARIMA model implementation
* Forecasting future electricity consumption

---

## 🧠 Tech Stack

* Python
* Pandas, NumPy
* Statsmodels
* Matplotlib

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
Electricity-Consumption/
│
├── main.py
├── README.md
├── .gitignore
├── requirements.txt
├── images/
│   └── forecast.png
└── data/   (dataset should be placed here)
```

---

## 🚀 How to Run

```bash
git clone https://github.com/j-pavitr/Electricity-Consumption.git
cd Electricity-Consumption
pip install -r requirements.txt
python main.py
```

